c ElimLin depth fixture — 4-var, 3-poly system.
c Every equation shares the quadratic monomial x1*x2 but pairs off to different linear tails.
c XOR-ing rows in pairs (which is exactly Gauss-Jordan over GF(2) after treating x1*x2 as
c a single column) yields the linear equations
c   row1 XOR row2 = x2 + x3       -> equivalence x(3) + x(2)
c   row1 XOR row3 = x1 + x4       -> equivalence x(4) + x(1)
c Trivial linear substitution alone cannot recover either because the input has no linear
c polynomials to substitute FROM. --el 1 is required.
x1*x2 + x1 + x2
x1*x2 + x1 + x3
x1*x2 + x2 + x4
